    rdfs:comment "1998 book by Paul Cilliers (Routledge), cited in Frankly_138's show notes alongside the episode's complex-systems-thinking discussion. Author/title NOT independently re-verified this session — taken directly from the official show notes' own citation, which is itself a stronger source than an unverified transcript mention."@en ;
    .

tgs:Work.GlobalTippingPointsReport2025 a thinkr:Work, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Global Tipping Points Report 2025"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Cited in Frankly_138's show notes specifically for its treatment of ice-sheet and soil-system tipping points. Full authorship/publisher NOT independently verified this session — real, citable report per the official show notes' own link, worth a proper WebFetch verification pass before treating this stub as complete."@en ;
    .

#############################################
# ADDED 2026-08-13 — surfaced via Frankly_20's real linked show notes.
#############################################

tgs:Work.RealityBlind a thinkr:Work, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Reality Blind: Integrating the Systems Science Underpinning Our Collective Futures, Vol. 1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Co-authored by Nate Hagens and DJ White (now a real, built Persona in this graph — resolves a note in an earlier, since-consolidated version of this entry flagging he wasn't yet modeled). Self-published on Amazon (ISBN 9798701116281) specifically so full content could stay free online — was the primary text for Hagens' own 'Reality 101' class. Covers deep time, human brain/behavior, ecology, and energy/money/economy, including a real elaboration of Concept.CarbonPulse (already in this graph) as a central framing device. Confirmed via multiple independent sources: Amazon, Goodreads, a LinkedIn post from Nate himself, MAHB, Stanford."@en ;
    dct:issued "2021"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dct:creator tgs:Human.NateHagens, tgs:Human.DJWhite ;
    dct:source <https://read.realityblind.world/> ;
    thinkr:hasAlternateTerm [ a thinkr:AlternateTerm ;
        thinkr:hasAlternateTermType tgs:AlternateTermType.ExactMatch ;
        skos:prefLabel "Reality Blind"@en ;
        skos:scopeNote "Short-form title, used in casual reference (e.g. this graph's own dct:references usage) versus the full formal title." ] ;
    .

#############################################
# ADDED 2026-08-13 — RR-26 Tier 3 enrichment, surfaced via its own real
# linked show notes.
#############################################

tgs:Work.Combining a thinkr:Work, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Combining"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Author: Nora Bateson. Published September 2023 by Triarchy Press, 386pp. A poetic, relational exploration of the ecology of communication and interdependency — introduces/elaborates 'Aphanipoiesis' (the unseen ways life comes together) and connects to her earlier-coined 'Warm Data.'"@en ;
    dct:source <https://www.triarchypress.net/combining.html> ;
    .

tgs:Work.Belly a thinkr:Work, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Belly"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Author: Nora Bateson. Published September 1, 2026 by Triarchy Press. Described by its own publisher as 'a cookbook for life' — an exploration of nth-order effects and 'the among-ing of all life' through food, family, illness, migration, and ecology."@en ;
    dct:source <https://www.triarchypress.net/belly.html> ;
    .

